  "scientific_review": [
    "The new method was declared and documented before deeper diagnostic outcomes were computed. Menze et al.(2019)20–500m averaged current maps provide context for an OSW exploratory selection interval; source summer2014–2017 observations do not independently validate the broader73–79.6N reach,2022 dates,model axes or winter flow. Neither500m nor the published isobaths is treated as a current bottom.",
    "All16 original WSC source sections and their full native columns remain unchanged. Frozen original surface diagnoses are recomputed and audited before reanalysis. Native20m/500m endpoints and complete finite interval support are required; positive signed trapezoidal integral and an interval maximum strictly above10cm/s qualify a column. No surface velocity is required. First western index breaks ties. Edge/support-edge winners remain unresolved rather than being replaced by weaker interior columns.",
    "Frozen connected-layer calculations use each5/10/20cm/s cutoff own seed within20–500m, then follow the complete native0–5000m support upward/downward. A lower crossing can lie below500m. Missing/dry support and sampled edges censor boundaries; the surface becomes a zero top only with connected support reaching it. Upper depth,lower depth,brackets,statuses,supported-reach bounds and paired span remain distinct. Lower depth is not silently used as thickness.",
    "The thin derived report records every candidate,selection and contour with original source byte hashes and original surface-selected index/diagnosis reference. Raw velocity/profile pointers target immutable original source files; derived contour pointers target the new report. No duplicate source velocity arrays or relabeled original diagnoses are published.",
    "Frozen adjacent-only interpolation preserves every original anchor and all selection/depth gaps. Unselected reference midpoints remain explicitly unsampled. Primary censoring is not filled by another cutoff; no gap skipping,extrapolation,gate change or seasonal continuity is forced. Reference connector lengths remain separate from measured current lengths.",
    "The comparison group model_interval20_500_no_surface_gate and distinct method IDs separate these results from surface-screened cases. Both diagnostics use the same dated model fields and are not independent evidence. They must not be pooled into apparently observed annual ranges. Existing84 scenarios,historical unresolved cases,all earlier CSV cells and canonical depth-reference ownership lists are preserved by cloud checks.",
    "Thirty cloud tests in groups12/10/8 cover frozen layers,new interval invariants and the full source-to-inventory pipeline. Tests cover opposing/missing surface support,nonzero upper depth,lower crossings below500m,censoring,native endpoints,signed scores,ties and edge selection,source/derived mutation rejection,correct separate pointers,all16cases,old CSV/ownership preservation,piece/count integrity and fixed caps. Six canonical baseline tests passed on the same code commit.",
    "All profile calculations,source audits,geometry,interpolation,inventory reconstruction and tests ran sequentially in the cloud on one idle CPU. Local work was source-text/metadata review,code preparation,hash verification and exact artifact retention. No new provider field retrieval,local numerical field processing/tests or runtime/UI/browser execution occurred. Original transport/publication caps remain unchanged.",
    "No Atlantic Water temperature/salinity gate,bathymetric current axis,independent named-current identity,physical whole-current thickness,annual envelope,matched width-depth area,volume,state join or global total is admitted. Same-sign deep flow and adjacent branches remain identification limitations. Coverage across the remaining71current identities and complete physical route depths remain unfinished."
  ],
